<%# S3c T3: the artefact lane's ONE refusal (plan §8.1, §8.2).

    Deliberately the same answer for all three ways to get here: an unknown kind,
    a project of another organisation, and a project whose booked time this reader
    may not see. The address is typeable, so a message that told them apart would
    be an existence oracle about other people's projects.

    Not a 403 page and not an empty lane either: the panel says, in one sentence,
    that there is nothing here for this reader.

    target and class below are repeated from the shell's frame for the case where
    somebody opens this address directly. They do NOT reach the panel: Turbo swaps
    only the children of the frame that is already in the document, so the owner
    of both is layouts/_assistant_panel. %>
<%= turbo_frame_tag 'assistant_panel_artefact', target: '_top', class: 'assistant-lane-artefact min-h-0' do %>
  <div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-2 px-4 py-3 border-b-2 border-cream-300">
    <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-cream-900 truncate">
      <%= t('views.organisations.assistant_artefacts.unavailable.title') %>
    </h3>
    <button type="button"
            data-action="assistant-panel#closeArtefact"
            title="<%= t('views.organisations.assistant_artefacts.shell.close') %>"
            aria-label="<%= t('views.organisations.assistant_artefacts.shell.close') %>"
            class="w-7 h-7 shrink-0 flex items-center justify-center text-cream-500 hover:text-cream-900 hover:bg-cream-200 rounded transition-all">
      <i class="bi bi-x-lg text-sm"></i>
    </button>
  </div>
  <p class="p-4 text-sm text-cream-600">
    <%= t('views.organisations.assistant_artefacts.unavailable.body') %>
  </p>
<% end %>
